Polypiling does still help.

: ***SPOILERS ALERT *** may be minor
: 

: Once I piled about 20 scrolls and other misc. stuff and polymorphed it. The
: result was one straw golem and other misc., stuff. All the spell books and
: scrolls were gone. 

I once got a leather golem, and another time an iron golem.

: Writing on blank spellbooks require huge amounts of ink. "identify" took
: 43 charges out of my magic marker once. One interesting thing was when the
: marker ran out of ink, the spell book was left "unfinished". Wonder I could 
: recharge the marker and continue writing.

Yes you can recharge a magic marker, but not forever.

: Rereading spellbooks makes them blank at a rate determined by the spell level.
: The "identify" spellbook bacame blank only after 4 readings whereas "sleep"
: spellbook is still readable after 12 readings.

Finger of death and cancellation go blank in 1.

: falling in to a moat causes all (almost) of scrolls, potions, books to become
: blank. But I got saved once even when the teleport didn't work. 
: I guess this is balanced by the new "amulet of magical breathing".

When you walk into lava, to retrieve some items, you risk losing stuff as
well.

: Wishing for named weapons is a bit risky. Once I asked for "magicbane" and got
: just that. The real one was called "Magicbane". This can be verified via an id
: scroll though. It says "the Magicbane" instead of "an athame called magicbane"
: This is one cool weapon IMHO.

Unique named weapons skip the "weapon called" part and start with the
word "the".  Named weapons which aren't unique (like Sting) are called a
runed dagger called Sting.

: Whats with the new medusa level. The only exit from the first room opens to a
: moat. I guess you need levitation/water walking to get past that.

 Further Spoilers
Nope.  When you get to this level a scroll of magic mapping will reveal
there is no entrace to the tower from the outside, nor is there a
stairways down.

: Thats all for now. I was hoping to finish my thesis this semester. It looks
